<title>USA: Intl Communications holders approve split.</title>
<headline>Intl Communications holders approve split.</headline>
<dateline>JACKSONVILLE, Fla. 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>International Communications and Technologies Corp said Thursday that last month holders of a majority of its shares approved the reverse-split of issued and outstanding common stock.</p>
<p>The company issued a statement saying the holders implemented a reverse-split on the basis of one new share for every 50 issued and outstanding shares of record on May 9.</p>
<p>The split and the decision to change the company's name to GBS Com-Tech Corp were effective May 15, the company said.</p>
